title: Rex::LibSSH's next release verifies host keys by default (CWE-322) — check
  Hetzner provisioning flow
updated: 2026-09-20T19:51:42Z
---

Rex::LibSSH gets a new default in its next release: the server host key is verified against known_hosts before authentication (CWE-322 fix). Freshly provisioned Hetzner dedicated servers are never in known_hosts, so the first connection in a deploy task can fail with a host-key error after a Rex::LibSSH upgrade.

Before bumping Rex::LibSSH here, check the provisioning flow: either ssh-keyscan the box into known_hosts first, or set an explicit opt-out (strict_hostkeycheck => 0 per connection, or -feature => ['disable_strict_host_key_checking'] Rexfile-wide).

Source: rex-libssh pre-release audit (HEAD 7085c0f). Not yet released.

